Regression test: sd document view accessible disposed while a call waits for the SolarMutex.

Same race as the slide sorter (hst-sd-slidesorter-a11y-lock-order.patch): the gtk3 accessibility
bridge calls in from the main loop without the SolarMutex while another thread holding it disposes
the document view. The test holds the SolarMutex, starts getAccessibleChildCount,
getAccessibleChild, getAccessibleAtPoint or getBackground of the Draw document view on another
thread, disposes the view and expects DisposedException.

License: the new test file is HST-owned (LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary); the makefile keeps MPL-2.0.
Test: CppunitTest_sd_a11y.
---
--- a/sd/CppunitTest_sd_a11y.mk
+++ b/sd/CppunitTest_sd_a11y.mk
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 $(eval $(call gb_CppunitTest_add_exception_objects,sd_a11y, \
 	sd/qa/unit/a11y/layout \
 	sd/qa/unit/a11y/HstSlideSorterDisposeRace \
+	sd/qa/unit/a11y/HstDocumentViewDisposeRace \
 ))
 
 $(eval $(call gb_CppunitTest_use_libraries,sd_a11y, \
--- /dev/null
+++ b/sd/qa/unit/a11y/HstDocumentViewDisposeRace.cxx
@@ -0,0 +1,145 @@
+/* -*- Mode: C++; tab-width: 4; indent-tabs-mode: nil; c-basic-offset: 4; fill-column: 100 -*- */
+/*
